/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Ezekiel chapters 41-45 */
VG.registerBibleChapters("ezekiel", [
{n:41, name:"The Temple Measured", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 41:4",verse:"So he measured the length thereof, twenty cubits; and the breadth, twenty cubits, before the temple: and he said unto me, This is the most holy place."}, facts:["Did you know the most holy place in Ezekiel's vision is a perfect square, twenty cubits by twenty, and the guide announces it with the words, 'This is the most holy place' (Ezekiel 41:4)?","Did you know the temple walls were carved with cherubim that each had two faces, a man's and a young lion's, with a palm tree standing between every pair (Ezekiel 41:18-19)?","Did you know the side chambers around the temple rose in three stacked stories, thirty chambers in all, with a winding stair that grew wider as it climbed (Ezekiel 41:6-7)?"], questions:[
{q:"How broad were the posts of the temple on each side?", options:["Six cubits broad on the one side, and six cubits on the other","Three cubits on each side","Ten cubits on each side","One reed on each side"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:1",verse:"Afterward he brought me to the temple, and measured the posts, six cubits broad on the one side, and six cubits broad on the other side, which was the breadth of the tabernacle.", insight:"God measures what He means to fill; every cubit of the temple says He takes His dwelling seriously."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of the temple itself?", options:["Forty cubits long and twenty cubits broad","Twenty cubits long and ten broad","Sixty cubits long and thirty broad","A hundred cubits long and broad"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:2",verse:"And the breadth of the door was ten cubits; and the sides of the door were five cubits on the one side, and five cubits on the other side: and he measured the length thereof, forty cubits: and the breadth, twenty cubits.", insight:"Forty by twenty, with a ten-cubit door; God's house is built to a pattern, not to human guesswork."},
{q:"How wide was the inner door that the man measured?", options:["Seven cubits","Six cubits","Two cubits","Ten cubits"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:3",verse:"Then went he inward, and measured the post of the door, two cubits; and the door, six cubits; and the breadth of the door, seven cubits.", insight:"Even the inner door is measured; nothing in God's presence is left to chance."},
{q:"What were the measurements of the most holy place?", options:["Twenty cubits long and twenty cubits broad","Ten cubits by ten cubits","Forty cubits by twenty cubits","Six cubits by six cubits"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:4",verse:"So he measured the length thereof, twenty cubits; and the breadth, twenty cubits, before the temple: and he said unto me, This is the most holy place.", insight:"The most holy place is a perfect square; God's holiness is complete on every side."},
{q:"How broad was every side chamber round about the house?", options:["Four cubits","Six cubits","Five cubits","Three cubits"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:5",verse:"After he measured the wall of the house, six cubits; and the breadth of every side chamber, four cubits, round about the house on every side.", insight:"Four-cubit chambers ring the house; God gives His servants a place close to His presence."},
{q:"How were the side chambers arranged?", options:["Three stories, one over another, thirty in order","Two stories, twenty in order","One story, forty in order","Four stories, twelve in order"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:6",verse:"And the side chambers were three, one over another, and thirty in order; and they entered into the wall which was of the house for the side chambers round about, that they might have hold, but they had not hold in the wall of the house.", insight:"Thirty chambers in three stories; there is room for many in the courts of the Lord."},
{q:"Why did the chambers grow broader as they went upward?", options:["The winding stair went still upward round the house, so the house widened toward the top","New walls were added to the upper rooms","The lower chambers were taken away","The foundation settled under the weight"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:7",verse:"And there was an enlarging, and a winding about still upward to the side chambers: for the winding about of the house went still upward round about the house: therefore the breadth of the house was still upward, and so increased from the lowest chamber to the highest by the midst.", insight:"The stair winds upward and grows wider; the way of God goes up, and it widens as you climb."},
{q:"How were the foundations of the side chambers measured?", options:["A full reed of six great cubits","Five ordinary cubits","Three hand breadths","One hundred reeds"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:8",verse:"I saw also the height of the house round about: the foundations of the side chambers were a full reed of six great cubits.", insight:"Great cubits for the foundation; what carries God's house must be built to last."},
{q:"How thick was the outer wall of the side chambers?", options:["Five cubits","Six cubits","Four cubits","Seven cubits"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:9",verse:"The thickness of the wall, which was for the side chamber without, was five cubits: and that which was left was the place of the side chambers that were within.", insight:"Five cubits thick; God guards the chambers of His house."},
{q:"Which way did the doors of the side chambers face?", options:["One door toward the north, and another toward the south","East and west","Toward the inner court only","Toward the porch"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:11",verse:"And the doors of the side chambers were toward the place that was left, one door toward the north, and another door toward the south: and the breadth of the place that was left was five cubits round about.", insight:"Doors to the north and south; God's house opens to His servants from every side."},
{q:"How large was the building before the separate place on the west?", options:["Seventy cubits broad and ninety cubits long","A hundred by a hundred","Fifty by fifty","Forty by twenty"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:12",verse:"Now the building that was before the separate place at the end toward the west was seventy cubits broad; and the wall of the building was five cubits thick round about, and the length thereof ninety cubits.", insight:"Seventy by ninety on the west; even the outer buildings are measured by heaven."},
{q:"How long was the house itself?", options:["A hundred cubits","Ninety cubits","Seventy cubits","Forty cubits"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:13",verse:"So he measured the house, an hundred cubits long; and the separate place, and the building, with the walls thereof, an hundred cubits long;", insight:"A hundred cubits long; the house of God is no small afterthought."},
{q:"What stood with the inner temple in the hundred-cubit measure?", options:["The porches of the court","The altar and the laver","The gates and the wall","The chambers and the stairs"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:15",verse:"And he measured the length of the building over against the separate place which was behind it, and the galleries thereof on the one side and on the other side, an hundred cubits, with the inner temple, and the porches of the court;", insight:"Inner temple and porches measured as one; worship and approach belong together."},
{q:"What covered the walls of the inner temple?", options:["Wood, from the ground up to the windows","Gold leaf","Cedar only at the door","Linen curtains"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:16",verse:"The door posts, and the narrow windows, and the galleries round about on their three stories, over against the door, cieled with wood round about, and from the ground up to the windows, and the windows were covered;", insight:"Wood from ground to window; God clothes His house with the work of men's hands, offered back to Him."},
{q:"What decoration alternated on the temple walls?", options:["Cherubim and palm trees","Lions and oxen","Stars and moons","Vines and grapes"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:18",verse:"And it was made with cherubims and palm trees, so that a palm tree was between a cherub and a cherub; and every cherub had two faces;", insight:"Cherubim and palms alternate; heaven's guardians and earth's fruitfulness stand side by side."},
{q:"What two faces did every cherub show?", options:["The face of a man and the face of a young lion","A man and an eagle","An ox and an eagle","A lion and an ox"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:19",verse:"So that the face of a man was toward the palm tree on the one side, and the face of a young lion toward the palm tree on the other side: it was made through all the house round about.", insight:"A man's face and a lion's face; wisdom and strength both serve in God's house."},
{q:"Where were the cherubim and palm trees carved?", options:["From the ground to above the door, on the wall of the temple","Only on the ceiling","On the altar","On the porch floor"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:20",verse:"From the ground unto above the door were cherubims and palm trees made, and on the wall of the temple.", insight:"Carved from ground to above the door; the walls themselves preach."},
{q:"How were the posts of the temple shaped?", options:["Squared","Round","Twisted","Fluted"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:21",verse:"The posts of the temple were squared, and the face of the sanctuary; the appearance of the one as the appearance of the other.", insight:"Squared posts, matching faces; God's house is built straight and true."},
{q:"What did the man call the altar of wood?", options:["The table that is before the LORD","The mercy seat","The golden lampstand","The altar of incense"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:22",verse:"The altar of wood was three cubits high, and the length thereof two cubits; and the corners thereof, and the length thereof, and the walls thereof, were of wood: and he said unto me, This is the table that is before the LORD.", insight:"A wooden table before the LORD; even simple wood becomes holy when set before Him."},
{q:"How were the doors of the temple made?", options:["Two leaves apiece, two turning leaves","One solid leaf each","Three leaves each","Hinged panels of brass"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 41:24",verse:"And the doors had two leaves apiece, two turning leaves; two leaves for the one door, and two leaves for the other door.", insight:"Turning leaves, two apiece; the doors of God's house move at His servants' touch."}
]},
{n:42, name:"The Priests' Chambers", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 42:20",verse:"He measured it by the four sides: it had a wall round about, five hundred reeds long, and five hundred broad, to make a separation between the sanctuary and the profane place."}, facts:["Did you know the priests had to change out of their holy linen garments before going out to the people, laying them in the holy chambers so the people would not be sanctified by their clothes (Ezekiel 42:14)?","Did you know the whole sanctuary district measured a perfect square, five hundred reeds by five hundred, walled to separate the sanctuary from the common ground (Ezekiel 42:16-20)?","Did you know the priests ate the most holy things, the meat offering, the sin offering, and the trespass offering, in chambers set apart as holy (Ezekiel 42:13)?"], questions:[
{q:"Into which court did the man bring Ezekiel at the start of this chapter?", options:["The utter court, the way toward the north","The inner court","The temple porch","The east gate"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:1",verse:"Then he brought me forth into the utter court, the way toward the north: and he brought me into the chamber that was over against the separate place, and which was before the building toward the north.", insight:"Ezekiel is led to the outer court; God shows His servant every part of the house."},
{q:"What were the dimensions before the north door?", options:["A hundred cubits long and fifty broad","Fifty long and a hundred broad","Five hundred square","Twenty by ten"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:2",verse:"Before the length of an hundred cubits was the north door, and the breadth was fifty cubits.", insight:"A hundred by fifty; the priests' chambers are given generous measure."},
{q:"How was the walk before the chambers measured?", options:["Ten cubits broad inward, with a way of one cubit","Twenty cubits broad","One cubit broad","Fifty cubits broad"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:4",verse:"And before the chambers was a walk of ten cubits breadth inward, a way of one cubit; and their doors toward the north.", insight:"A ten-cubit walk before the doors; even the approach to holy rooms is ordered."},
{q:"Why were the upper chambers shorter than the lower ones?", options:["The galleries took more space from them than from the lower and middlemost","They had no windows","The wall was thinner there","They were left unfinished"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:5",verse:"Now the upper chambers were shorter: for the galleries were higher than these, than the lower, and than the middlemost of the building.", insight:"The upper rooms give way to the galleries; in God's house, every level has its place."},
{q:"How did the chamber building differ from the courts?", options:["It had no pillars, as the pillars of the courts","It had pillars of brass","It was roofed with gold","It stood upon the water"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:6",verse:"For they were in three stories, but had not pillars as the pillars of the courts: therefore the building was straitened more than the lowest and the middlemost from the ground.", insight:"No pillars like the courts; God varies His building, yet all of it stands."},
{q:"How long was the wall outside, before the chambers?", options:["Fifty cubits","A hundred cubits","Five hundred reeds","Twenty cubits"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:7",verse:"And the wall that was without over against the chambers, toward the utter court on the forepart of the chambers, the length thereof was fifty cubits.", insight:"Fifty cubits of wall; holiness is guarded, not careless."},
{q:"How long were the chambers in the utter court, and what lay before the temple?", options:["The chambers were fifty cubits, and a hundred cubits lay before the temple","Both were fifty cubits","The chambers were a hundred, the temple fifty","Both were a hundred cubits"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:8",verse:"For the length of the chambers that were in the utter court was fifty cubits: and, lo, before the temple were an hundred cubits.", insight:"Fifty for the chambers, a hundred before the temple; God proportions every space."},
{q:"From which side was the entry into the chambers?", options:["The east side, as one goes in from the utter court","The west side","The north gate","The inner court"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:9",verse:"And from under these chambers was the entry on the east side, as one goeth into them from the utter court.", insight:"The entry faces east; God's servants walk toward the light."},
{q:"What were the north and south chambers before the separate place called?", options:["Holy chambers","The king's chambers","Store chambers","The singers' chambers"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:13",verse:"Then said he unto me, The north chambers and the south chambers, which are before the separate place, they be holy chambers, where the priests that approach unto the LORD shall eat the most holy things: there shall they lay the most holy things, and the meat offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering; for the place is holy.", insight:"Holy chambers for holy work; some rooms are set apart for God alone."},
{q:"What did the priests eat in the holy chambers?", options:["The most holy things","Only bread","The Passover lamb","Fruit from the trees"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:13",verse:"Then said he unto me, The north chambers and the south chambers, which are before the separate place, they be holy chambers, where the priests that approach unto the LORD shall eat the most holy things: there shall they lay the most holy things, and the meat offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering; for the place is holy.", insight:"The priests eat the most holy things; those who serve God are fed by God."},
{q:"What were the priests forbidden to do when leaving the holy place?", options:["Go out into the utter court in the garments wherein they ministered","Eat the offerings","Speak to the people","Enter the temple"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:14",verse:"When the priests enter therein, then shall they not go out of the holy place into the utter court, but there they shall lay their garments wherein they minister; for they are holy; and shall put on other garments, and shall approach to those things which are for the people.", insight:"Holy garments stay in the holy place; what is worn before God is not worn casually."},
{q:"What did the priests do with their garments before approaching the people?", options:["Laid them in the holy chambers and put on other garments","Washed them in the river","Burned them","Gave them to the Levites"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:14",verse:"When the priests enter therein, then shall they not go out of the holy place into the utter court, but there they shall lay their garments wherein they minister; for they are holy; and shall put on other garments, and shall approach to those things which are for the people.", insight:"They change before meeting the people; reverence for God shapes how we meet men."},
{q:"Which way did the doors of the chambers face?", options:["Toward the north","Toward the south","Toward the east","Toward the west"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:4",verse:"And before the chambers was a walk of ten cubits breadth inward, a way of one cubit; and their doors toward the north.", insight:"Doors facing north; every chamber looks toward its appointed way."},
{q:"After measuring the inner house, to which gate was Ezekiel brought?", options:["The gate whose prospect is toward the east","The north gate","The west gate","The gate of the inner court"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:15",verse:"Now when he had made an end of measuring the inner house, he brought me forth toward the gate whose prospect is toward the east, and measured it round about.", insight:"The east gate comes last; God finishes His measuring where His glory entered."},
{q:"How far did the east side measure?", options:["Five hundred reeds","Five hundred cubits","A hundred cubits","Fifty reeds"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:16",verse:"He measured the east side with the measuring reed, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed round about.", insight:"Five hundred reeds to the east; God's sanctuary has wide borders."},
{q:"How far did the north side measure?", options:["Five hundred reeds","Four hundred reeds","Five hundred cubits","A hundred reeds"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:17",verse:"He measured the north side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed round about.", insight:"The same to the north; God's measure does not change with direction."},
{q:"How far did the south side measure?", options:["Five hundred reeds","Four hundred reeds","Five hundred cubits","Fifty reeds"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:18",verse:"He measured the south side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed.", insight:"Five hundred to the south as well; the square is complete on every side."},
{q:"What did the man measure when he turned to the west side?", options:["Five hundred reeds","Five hundred cubits","A hundred reeds","Nothing; he stopped measuring"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:19",verse:"He turned about to the west side, and measured five hundred reeds with the measuring reed.", insight:"And five hundred to the west; God's holiness is fenced round about."},
{q:"What was the whole measured square?", options:["Five hundred reeds long and five hundred broad","Five hundred cubits square","A thousand reeds square","A hundred cubits square"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:20",verse:"He measured it by the four sides: it had a wall round about, five hundred reeds long, and five hundred broad, to make a separation between the sanctuary and the profane place.", insight:"A perfect square, five hundred by five hundred; God's dwelling is ordered and complete."},
{q:"What was the purpose of the wall round about?", options:["To make a separation between the sanctuary and the profane place","To keep out enemies","To hold up the chambers","To mark the city boundary"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 42:20",verse:"He measured it by the four sides: it had a wall round about, five hundred reeds long, and five hundred broad, to make a separation between the sanctuary and the profane place.", insight:"A wall between the sanctuary and the common; God teaches His people to tell holy from ordinary."}
]},
{n:43, name:"The Glory Returns", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 43:5",verse:"So the spirit took me up, and brought me into the inner court; and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house."}, facts:["Did you know the glory of the LORD entered the new temple through the east gate, the same direction from which it had departed in Ezekiel's earlier vision (Ezekiel 43:2-4)?","Did you know God's voice in this vision sounded like a noise of many waters, and the earth itself shined with His glory (Ezekiel 43:2)?","Did you know the new altar was consecrated over seven days of sin offerings, and on the eighth day God said, 'I will accept you' (Ezekiel 43:26-27)?"], questions:[
{q:"To which gate was Ezekiel brought at the start of this chapter?", options:["The gate that looketh toward the east","The north gate","The west gate","The inner gate"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:1",verse:"Afterward he brought me to the gate, even the gate that looketh toward the east:", insight:"Ezekiel is brought to the east gate; what left by the east now returns by the east."},
{q:"From which direction did the glory of the God of Israel come?", options:["From the way of the east","From the north","From above the temple","From the sea"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:2",verse:"And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel came from the way of the east: and his voice was like a noise of many waters: and the earth shined with his glory.", insight:"The glory comes from the east; God returns the way He departed."},
{q:"What was His voice like?", options:["Like a noise of many waters","Like thunder in the hills","Like a trumpet blast","Like a still whisper"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:2",verse:"And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel came from the way of the east: and his voice was like a noise of many waters: and the earth shined with his glory.", insight:"A voice like many waters; when God speaks, all other sounds grow small."},
{q:"By which gate did the glory of the LORD come into the house?", options:["The gate whose prospect is toward the east","The north gate","The gate of the inner court","The porch gate"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:4",verse:"And the glory of the LORD came into the house by the way of the gate whose prospect is toward the east.", insight:"The glory enters by the east gate; God's presence takes the straight road home."},
{q:"What did Ezekiel do when the glory appeared?", options:["He fell upon his face","He ran to the gate","He covered his eyes and sang","He stood and prophesied"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:3",verse:"And it was according to the appearance of the vision which I saw, even according to the vision that I saw when I came to destroy the city: and the visions were like the vision that I saw by the river Chebar; and I fell upon my face.", insight:"Ezekiel falls on his face; glory always brings God's servants low before it lifts them."},
{q:"Which earlier visions was this appearance like?", options:["The vision when he came to destroy the city, and the vision by the river Chebar","The valley of dry bones","The wheel within a wheel only","The siege of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:3",verse:"And it was according to the appearance of the vision which I saw, even according to the vision that I saw when I came to destroy the city: and the visions were like the vision that I saw by the river Chebar; and I fell upon my face.", insight:"The same visions as Chebar and the city's fall; God is consistent in judgment and in mercy."},
{q:"Where did the Spirit bring Ezekiel?", options:["Into the inner court","To the Mount of Olives","Back to Babylon","To the outer gate"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:5",verse:"So the spirit took me up, and brought me into the inner court; and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house.", insight:"The Spirit lifts him into the inner court; we enter God's presence by the Spirit, not by striving."},
{q:"What filled the house?", options:["The glory of the LORD","A cloud of incense","The sound of singing","The priests"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:5",verse:"So the spirit took me up, and brought me into the inner court; and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house.", insight:"The glory filled the house; where God dwells, He fills."},
{q:"What did God call the house?", options:["The place of My throne, and the place of the soles of My feet","The house of sacrifice","The gate of heaven","The city of David"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:7",verse:"And he said unto me, Son of man, the place of my throne, and the place of the soles of my feet, where I will dwell in the midst of the children of Israel for ever, and my holy name, shall the house of Israel no more defile, neither they, nor their kings, by their whoredom, nor by the carcases of their kings in their high places.", insight:"The place of His throne and the soles of His feet; heaven's King chooses to dwell with men."},
{q:"How long would God dwell in the midst of Israel there?", options:["For ever","For forty years","For a thousand years","Until the exile ended"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:7",verse:"And he said unto me, Son of man, the place of my throne, and the place of the soles of my feet, where I will dwell in the midst of the children of Israel for ever, and my holy name, shall the house of Israel no more defile, neither they, nor their kings, by their whoredom, nor by the carcases of their kings in their high places.", insight:"Forever; God's dwelling with His people is not a visit but a home."},
{q:"How had Israel set their worship against God's?", options:["Their threshold by His thresholds, and their post by His posts, with a wall between","They built a higher altar","They sang louder songs","They came only at midnight"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:8",verse:"In their setting of their threshold by my thresholds, and their post by my posts, and the wall between me and them, they have even defiled my holy name by their abominations that they have committed: wherefore I have consumed them in mine anger.", insight:"Their threshold beside His threshold; Israel had crowded God to the edge of His own house."},
{q:"What must Israel put far away from God?", options:["Their whoredom, and the carcasses of their kings","Their gold and silver","Their walled cities","Their vineyards"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:9",verse:"Now let them put away their whoredom, and the carcases of their kings, far from me, and I will dwell in the midst of them for ever.", insight:"Put away the whoredom and the carcasses; God will not share His house with idols."},
{q:"Why was Ezekiel told to show the house to the house of Israel?", options:["That they may be ashamed of their iniquities","To make them proud","To find builders for it","To count the cost of it"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:10",verse:"Thou son of man, shew the house to the house of Israel, that they may be ashamed of their iniquities: and let them measure the pattern.", insight:"Show them the house, that they may be ashamed; seeing God's holiness exposes our sin."},
{q:"What were they to do with the pattern of the house?", options:["Measure it","Burn it","Hide it","Sell it"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:10",verse:"Thou son of man, shew the house to the house of Israel, that they may be ashamed of their iniquities: and let them measure the pattern.", insight:"Measure the pattern; God's design is given to be studied and kept."},
{q:"What is the law of the house?", options:["Upon the top of the mountain, the whole limit thereof round about shall be most holy","No stranger may ever enter","The priests must fast","The gates must stay open"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:12",verse:"This is the law of the house; Upon the top of the mountain the whole limit thereof round about shall be most holy. Behold, this is the law of the house.", insight:"The whole limit round about most holy; where God dwells, everything nearby is consecrated."},
{q:"How long and broad was the altar?", options:["Twelve cubits long and twelve broad, square","Fourteen by fourteen","Ten by ten","Twenty by twenty"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:16",verse:"And the altar shall be twelve cubits long, twelve broad, square in the four squares thereof.", insight:"Twelve by twelve, square; the altar of the new house stands foursquare and firm."},
{q:"How many horns rose from the altar upward?", options:["Four","Two","Seven","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:15",verse:"So the altar shall be four cubits; and from the altar and upward shall be four horns.", insight:"Four horns; strength and refuge rise from the altar of God."},
{q:"Which way did the stairs of the altar face?", options:["Toward the east","Toward the west","Toward the north","Toward the south"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:17",verse:"And the settle shall be fourteen cubits long and fourteen broad in the four squares thereof; and the border about it shall be half a cubit; and the bottom thereof shall be a cubit about; and his stairs shall look toward the east.", insight:"The stairs face east; the way up to God's altar looks toward the coming glory."},
{q:"Which priests were to minister at the altar?", options:["The priests the Levites, of the seed of Zadok","The sons of Aaron only","The Levites who went astray","The elders of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:19",verse:"And thou shalt give to the priests the Levites that be of the seed of Zadok, which approach unto me, to minister unto me, saith the Lord GOD, a young bullock for a sin offering.", insight:"The sons of Zadok, who stayed faithful; God honors loyalty in dark times."},
{q:"What did God promise when the offerings began on the eighth day?", options:["I will accept you","I will leave you","I will test you","I will hide from you"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 43:27",verse:"And when these days are expired, it shall be, that upon the eighth day, and so forward, the priests shall make your burnt offerings upon the altar, and your peace offerings; and I will accept you, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"On the eighth day, 'I will accept you'; all the cleansing ends in God's welcome."}
]},
{n:44, name:"The Shut Gate", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 44:28",verse:"And it shall be unto them for an inheritance: I am their inheritance: and ye shall give them no possession in Israel: I am their possession."}, facts:["Did you know the east gate was kept shut forever because the LORD had entered through it, and only the prince might sit in it to eat bread before Him (Ezekiel 44:2-3)?","Did you know the faithful priests wore linen from head to foot, even linen bonnets, and were forbidden anything that caused sweat, because their work was holy (Ezekiel 44:17-18)?","Did you know the priests owned no land in Israel; God said, 'I am their inheritance,' and they lived from the offerings and firstfruits (Ezekiel 44:28-30)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Ezekiel find at the east gate of the outward sanctuary?", options:["It was shut","It was open","It was broken","It was guarded by soldiers"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:1",verse:"Then he brought me back the way of the gate of the outward sanctuary which looketh toward the east; and it was shut.", insight:"The east gate stands shut; some doors close because God Himself has passed through."},
{q:"Why was the east gate to stay shut and never opened?", options:["Because the LORD, the God of Israel, had entered in by it","Because it was broken","Because the prince lived there","Because of the Sabbath"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:2",verse:"Then said the LORD unto me; This gate shall be shut, it shall not be opened, and no man shall enter in by it; because the LORD, the God of Israel, hath entered in by it, therefore it shall be shut.", insight:"No man may open what God has sealed; His entrance hallows the gate forever."},
{q:"Who alone might use the shut east gate?", options:["The prince, to sit in it and eat bread before the LORD","The high priest","The singers","No one at all"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:3",verse:"It is for the prince; the prince, he shall sit in it to eat bread before the LORD; he shall enter by the way of the porch of that gate, and shall go out by the way of the same.", insight:"The prince may sit and eat bread there; honor in God's house is given, not taken."},
{q:"How would the prince enter and leave by that gate?", options:["By the way of the porch of the gate, going out by the same way","Through the north gate","Over the wall","By the stairs"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:3",verse:"It is for the prince; the prince, he shall sit in it to eat bread before the LORD; he shall enter by the way of the porch of that gate, and shall go out by the way of the same.", insight:"In and out by the same porch; even the prince follows the appointed way."},
{q:"What did Ezekiel see when he was brought by the north gate?", options:["The glory of the LORD filled the house of the LORD","An empty temple","The prince feasting","The Levites singing"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:4",verse:"Then brought he me the way of the north gate before the house: and I looked, and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house of the LORD: and I fell upon my face.", insight:"The glory fills the house again; Ezekiel falls, as every seer of glory must."},
{q:"What three things was Ezekiel told to do with the ordinances?", options:["Mark well, behold with his eyes, and hear with his ears","Write, sing, and dance","Measure, weigh, and count","Ask, seek, and knock"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:5",verse:"And the LORD said unto me, Son of man, mark well, and behold with thine eyes, and hear with thine ears all that I say unto thee concerning all the ordinances of the house of the LORD, and all the laws thereof; and mark well the entering in of the house, with every going forth of the sanctuary.", insight:"Mark well, see, and hear; God's ordinances deserve our full attention."},
{q:"How did God address the house of Israel?", options:["The rebellious","The chosen remnant","The faithful","The strangers"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:6",verse:"And thou shalt say to the rebellious, even to the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; O ye house of Israel, let it suffice you of all your abominations,", insight:"God calls them rebellious; He names our sin plainly because He means to heal it."},
{q:"What had Israel brought into the sanctuary?", options:["Strangers, uncircumcised in heart and uncircumcised in flesh","Gold from Egypt","Idols of wood","Foreign priests"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:7",verse:"In that ye have brought into my sanctuary strangers, uncircumcised in heart, and uncircumcised in flesh, to be in my sanctuary, to pollute it, even my house, when ye offer my bread, the fat and the blood, and they have broken my covenant because of all your abominations.", insight:"Strangers uncircumcised in heart; outward ritual never substitutes for an inward covenant."},
{q:"What rule was given about strangers and the sanctuary?", options:["No stranger, uncircumcised in heart or in flesh, shall enter into My sanctuary","They must pay a tax","They may enter on feast days","They must be circumcised in flesh only"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:9",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; No stranger, uncircumcised in heart, nor uncircumcised in flesh, shall enter into my sanctuary, of any stranger that is among the children of Israel.", insight:"No stranger shall enter; God's sanctuary is guarded for those in covenant."},
{q:"What would happen to the Levites who went far from God after idols?", options:["They shall bear their iniquity","They would die at once","They would be exiled","They would be fully forgiven"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:10",verse:"And the Levites that are gone away far from me, when Israel went astray, which went astray away from me after their idols; they shall even bear their iniquity.", insight:"The straying Levites bear their iniquity; choices have consequences, even for ministers."},
{q:"What service was left to the unfaithful Levites?", options:["Keepers of the charge of the house, for all the service thereof","Priests of the most holy place","Judges of the people","Sole keepers of the gates"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:14",verse:"But I will make them keepers of the charge of the house, for all the service thereof, and for all that shall be done therein.", insight:"Keepers of the charge, but not priests; mercy keeps them serving, justice keeps them from the altar."},
{q:"What were they barred from?", options:["Coming near to do the office of a priest, or to the holy things of the most holy place","Entering the city","Eating bread","Teaching the people"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:13",verse:"And they shall not come near unto me, to do the office of a priest unto me, nor to come near to any of my holy things, in the most holy place: but they shall bear their shame, and their abominations which they have committed.", insight:"Barred from the most holy; nearness to God is a privilege, not a right."},
{q:"Which priests would come near to minister to God?", options:["The priests the Levites, the sons of Zadok, who kept the charge when Israel went astray","The sons of Aaron who stayed in Egypt","The Levites who repented","The elders of the people"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:15",verse:"But the priests the Levites, the sons of Zadok, that kept the charge of my sanctuary when the children of Israel went astray from me, they shall come near to me to minister unto me, and they shall stand before me to offer unto me the fat and the blood, saith the Lord GOD:", insight:"The sons of Zadok stayed faithful when others strayed; God remembers steadfastness."},
{q:"What were the priests to wear when entering the inner court?", options:["Linen garments, with no wool upon them","Wool robes","Sackcloth","Purple and scarlet"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:17",verse:"And it shall come to pass, that when they enter in at the gates of the inner court, they shall be clothed with linen garments; and no wool shall come upon them, whiles they minister in the gates of the inner court, and within.", insight:"Linen, no wool; those who minister to God wear what befits His presence."},
{q:"What were they forbidden to gird themselves with?", options:["Any thing that causeth sweat","Gold","Swords","Bells"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:18",verse:"They shall have linen bonnets upon their heads, and shall have linen breeches upon their loins; they shall not gird themselves with any thing that causeth sweat.", insight:"Nothing that causes sweat; God's service is not done in the heat of human striving."},
{q:"How were the priests to wear their hair?", options:["Neither shave their heads, nor let their locks grow long; only poll them","Shave them bald","Let them grow long","Cover them always"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:20",verse:"Neither shall they shave their heads, nor suffer their locks to grow long; they shall only poll their heads.", insight:"Neither shaved nor overgrown; even a priest's haircut preaches order."},
{q:"What was forbidden to any priest entering the inner court?", options:["Drinking wine","Eating bread","Wearing sandals","Speaking aloud"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:21",verse:"Neither shall any priest drink wine, when they enter into the inner court.", insight:"No wine in the inner court; clear heads for holy work."},
{q:"Whom could a priest not take for a wife?", options:["A widow, nor her that is put away","A maiden of Israel","A widow that had a priest before","A Levite's daughter"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:22",verse:"Neither shall they take for their wives a widow, nor her that is put away: but they shall take maidens of the seed of the house of Israel, or a widow that had a priest before.", insight:"A priest's home must match his calling; even marriage answers to holiness."},
{q:"What were the priests to teach the people?", options:["The difference between the holy and profane, and between the unclean and the clean","The law of Moses only","Songs of the temple","The history of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:23",verse:"And they shall teach my people the difference between the holy and profane, and cause them to discern between the unclean and the clean.", insight:"Teach holy from profane; God's people must learn to tell the difference."},
{q:"What was the priests' inheritance?", options:["The LORD Himself: 'I am their inheritance'","The land around the temple","The city of Jerusalem","Gold from the offerings"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 44:28",verse:"And it shall be unto them for an inheritance: I am their inheritance: and ye shall give them no possession in Israel: I am their possession.", insight:"'I am their inheritance'; when God is your portion, you lack nothing."}
]},
{n:45, name:"The Holy Portion", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 45:8",verse:"In the land shall be his possession in Israel: and my princes shall no more oppress my people; and the rest of the land shall they give to the house of Israel according to their tribes."}, facts:["Did you know the holy district was a vast rectangle, twenty-five thousand reeds long, with the sanctuary, the priests' land, the Levites' chambers, the city, and the prince's portion all laid out by God's own survey (Ezekiel 45:1-7)?","Did you know God commanded 'just balances, and a just ephah, and a just bath,' making honest trade a matter of holiness, and defined the shekel as twenty gerahs (Ezekiel 45:10-12)?","Did you know the prince himself had to provide a bullock as a sin offering on Passover day, for himself and for all the people of the land (Ezekiel 45:22)?"], questions:[
{q:"How was the land to be divided for inheritance?", options:["By lot","By the prince's decree","By battle","By purchase"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:1",verse:"Moreover, when ye shall divide by lot the land for inheritance, ye shall offer an oblation unto the LORD, an holy portion of the land: the length shall be the length of five and twenty thousand reeds, and the breadth shall be ten thousand. This shall be holy in all the borders thereof round about.", insight:"The land divided by lot; God Himself apportions the inheritance."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of the holy portion offered to the LORD?", options:["Five and twenty thousand reeds long, and ten thousand broad","Five hundred by five hundred","Ten thousand square","Twenty thousand by five thousand"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:1",verse:"Moreover, when ye shall divide by lot the land for inheritance, ye shall offer an oblation unto the LORD, an holy portion of the land: the length shall be the length of five and twenty thousand reeds, and the breadth shall be ten thousand. This shall be holy in all the borders thereof round about.", insight:"Twenty-five thousand by ten thousand; the holy portion is measured large because God is generous."},
{q:"How large was the sanctuary square within the holy portion?", options:["Five hundred in length, with five hundred in breadth","A thousand square","Fifty by fifty","A hundred square"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:2",verse:"Of this there shall be for the sanctuary five hundred in length, with five hundred in breadth, square round about; and fifty cubits round about for the suburbs thereof.", insight:"Five hundred square for the sanctuary; God's own house sits at the center of the land."},
{q:"For whom was the holy portion of the land set apart?", options:["The priests, the ministers of the sanctuary","The prince","The whole house of Israel","The Levites"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:4",verse:"The holy portion of the land shall be for the priests the ministers of the sanctuary, which shall come near to minister unto the LORD: and it shall be a place for their houses, and an holy place for the sanctuary.", insight:"The holy portion for the priests; those who minister to God are provided for first."},
{q:"What portion did the Levites receive?", options:["Five and twenty thousand by ten thousand, for a possession for twenty chambers","The same as the priests","The city itself","The prince's land"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:5",verse:"And the five and twenty thousand of length, and the ten thousand of breadth, shall also the Levites, the ministers of the house, have for themselves, for a possession for twenty chambers.", insight:"Twenty chambers for the Levites; God's servants are housed by God's plan."},
{q:"What was appointed for the possession of the city?", options:["Five thousand broad and five and twenty thousand long, for the whole house of Israel","A square of five hundred","The east gate","Nothing at all"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:6",verse:"And ye shall appoint the possession of the city five thousand broad, and five and twenty thousand long, over against the oblation of the holy portion: it shall be for the whole house of Israel.", insight:"A city for the whole house of Israel; the holy land has room for all God's people."},
{q:"Where did the prince's portion lie?", options:["On the one side and on the other side of the holy oblation and the city, from the west border to the east border","North of the temple","Inside the city walls","Beyond the river"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:7",verse:"And a portion shall be for the prince on the one side and on the other side of the oblation of the holy portion, and of the possession of the city, before the oblation of the holy portion, and before the possession of the city, from the west side westward, and from the east side eastward: and the length shall be over against one of the portions, from the west border unto the east border.", insight:"The prince's portion flanks the holy ground; even rulers are set beside, not above, God's portion."},
{q:"What promise was given concerning the princes?", options:["They shall no more oppress My people","They would rule forever","They would build the temple","They would leave Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:8",verse:"In the land shall be his possession in Israel: and my princes shall no more oppress my people; and the rest of the land shall they give to the house of Israel according to their tribes.", insight:"Princes shall no more oppress; God's kingdom ends the abuse of power."},
{q:"What was the charge given to the princes of Israel?", options:["Remove violence and spoil, execute judgment and justice, take away your exactions","Build higher walls","Gather more taxes","Make war on the nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:9",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; Let it suffice you, O princes of Israel: remove violence and spoil, and execute judgment and justice, take away your exactions from my people, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"Remove violence, do justice; God commands rulers to rule righteously."},
{q:"What measures were the people commanded to have?", options:["Just balances, and a just ephah, and a just bath","Double weights","The king's measure","Egyptian standards"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:10",verse:"Ye shall have just balances, and a just ephah, and a just bath.", insight:"Just balances, just measures; honesty in trade is a holy duty."},
{q:"How did the ephah and the bath relate to the homer?", options:["Each was the tenth part of a homer","Each was half a homer","The ephah was double the bath","They were unrelated"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:11",verse:"The ephah and the bath shall be of one measure, that the bath may contain the tenth part of an homer, and the ephah the tenth part of an homer: the measure thereof shall be after the homer.", insight:"The bath and ephah match the homer; God's standard is one for all."},
{q:"How many gerahs made a shekel?", options:["Twenty","Ten","Twelve","Thirty"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:12",verse:"And the shekel shall be twenty gerahs: twenty shekels, five and twenty shekels, fifteen shekels, shall be your maneh.", insight:"Twenty gerahs to the shekel; even small coins are weighed by God's rule."},
{q:"What made up the maneh?", options:["Twenty shekels, five and twenty shekels, and fifteen shekels","Sixty shekels","Fifty shekels","A hundred gerahs"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:12",verse:"And the shekel shall be twenty gerahs: twenty shekels, five and twenty shekels, fifteen shekels, shall be your maneh.", insight:"The maneh defined; God leaves no measure vague."},
{q:"What was the oblation of wheat and barley?", options:["The sixth part of an ephah of a homer of each","A whole homer of each","A tenth of each","An ephah of each"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:13",verse:"This is the oblation that ye shall offer; the sixth part of an ephah of an homer of wheat, and ye shall give the sixth part of an ephah of an homer of barley:", insight:"A sixth of an ephah; giving to God is measured, regular, and fair."},
{q:"What was the ordinance of oil?", options:["The tenth part of a bath out of the cor","A whole bath","A hin","Half a bath"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:14",verse:"Concerning the ordinance of oil, the bath of oil, ye shall offer the tenth part of a bath out of the cor, which is an homer of ten baths; for ten baths are an homer:", insight:"A tenth of a bath of oil; the oil of gladness is offered by rule, not by whim."},
{q:"How many lambs were given for the offerings?", options:["One lamb out of two hundred, out of the fat pastures of Israel","One in ten","Seven daily","One in a thousand"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:15",verse:"And one lamb out of the flock, out of two hundred, out of the fat pastures of Israel; for a meat offering, and for a burnt offering, and for peace offerings, to make reconciliation for them, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"One lamb in two hundred; God's portion is modest, and it makes reconciliation."},
{q:"What was the prince's part in the feasts and solemnities?", options:["To give the burnt offerings, meat offerings, and drink offerings, and prepare the sacrifices for reconciliation","To offer nothing","To sing before the people","To guard the gates"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:17",verse:"And it shall be the prince’s part to give burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and drink offerings, in the feasts, and in the new moons, and in the sabbaths, in all solemnities of the house of Israel: he shall prepare the sin offering, and the meat offering, and the burnt offering, and the peace offerings, to make reconciliation for the house of Israel.", insight:"The prince provides the offerings; leadership means supplying worship, not just ruling."},
{q:"On what day was the sanctuary cleansed with a young bullock?", options:["The first day of the first month","The fourteenth day","The seventh day","The tenth day"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:18",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the first month, in the first day of the month, thou shalt take a young bullock without blemish, and cleanse the sanctuary:", insight:"The first day, the sanctuary cleansed; the year begins with purity."},
{q:"When was the Passover kept?", options:["The fourteenth day of the first month, a feast of seven days","The first day of the month","The fifteenth of the seventh month","The tenth day"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:21",verse:"In the first month, in the fourteenth day of the month, ye shall have the passover, a feast of seven days; unleavened bread shall be eaten.", insight:"Passover on the fourteenth day; God's old feast stands in the new land."},
{q:"What was kept on the fifteenth day of the seventh month?", options:["A feast of seven days, kept like the Passover offerings","The Day of Atonement","The new moon","The Sabbath year"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 45:25",verse:"In the seventh month, in the fifteenth day of the month, shall he do the like in the feast of the seven days, according to the sin offering, according to the burnt offering, and according to the meat offering, and according to the oil.", insight:"The seventh month feast kept the same; God's calendar does not change with the scenery."}
]}
]);
